## Implementation Phases

Describe how to build this incrementally, reducing risk and enabling early validation.

### Phase 1: Core Stream Broker (Week 1-2)
- Deploy broker cluster (3 nodes)
- Create topic management UI
- Build client libraries (Go, Python, JS)
- **Success Criteria**: Can ingest and subscribe to 10K events/sec

### Phase 2: Stream Processor (Week 3-4)
- Build processor runtime (stateless execution model)
- Implement declarative pipeline definitions
- Deploy 2-3 processor instances
- **Success Criteria**: Can apply transformations at 50K events/sec with <100ms latency

### Phase 3: Persistence & Storage (Week 5-6)
- Integrate hot/cold storage
- Build archival policies
- Implement retention cleanup
- **Success Criteria**: Data durability verified; archival tested

### Phase 4: Observability & Operations (Week 7-8)
- Build dashboards, alerts, runbooks
- Load test to 1M events/sec
- Conduct failure mode analysis
- **Success Criteria**: On-call engineer can troubleshoot autonomously

